ll in the Self-Assessment."}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}], "questions": [{"responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06re7pdf01.pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe8n5le01ob06re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you are reading this section of the IT blog, it is because you haven&rsquo;t understood what CRUD stands for or what the proper use of it is. Thus, throughout this section, we will briefly explain to you what CRUD stands for and what it is by answering questions like &ldquo;why are we using CRUD to create a database?&rdquo;, &ldquo;how is CRUD improving storage?&rdquo;, and &ldquo;are we working with the correct database?&rdquo;.</p>", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob06re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0}, {"text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If you haven&rsquo;t worked with databases before, it will be a little difficult to understand what CRUD is. However, in short, we can tell you it is a mnemonic for the four basic functions of persistent storage, that is, Create, Read, Update and Delete. Even though CRUD hasn&rsquo;t included any further function, it will allow the user to manipulate information in any database by adding new data into it or to retrieve information that was previously stored, so that the user can manipulate it, update it, or dispose of it when necessary. Hence, we can say CRUD functions have improved storage since they have mapped SQL statements to make databases work safe and sound from possible threats.</p>", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob06re2img02.jpg", "time": "24000", "id": 1}, {"text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Since we are working with SQL language, when we talk about CRUD, we can automatically relate it to stored procedures, which prevent hazards such as injection attacks that can either alter or delete our data. On the other hand, every time you work with databases, no matter what kind of database it is, you will always talk about CRUD functions which help to surf through the information that the user may require from the database.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">If, by now, you haven&rsquo;t understood the basics of CRUD, you can always check out the video tutorial section where you are going to find thousands of useful videos.</p>", "image": "enpe8n5le01ob06re2img03.jpg", "time": "71000", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe8n5le01ob06re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 1}, {"type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0}], "video_src": "enpe8n5le01ob06re5vsc01"}, "type": "video"}], "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "id": 4}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "CRUD Summary "}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about CRUD functions."}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Uses the four basic functions in persistent storage to create the system.   Talks about the four basic functions for persistent storage. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Reads and Writes effective texts in English showing good organisation and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context.   Writes simple texts on implementing web applications, using IT tools and building the functional phase of a project. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present perfect negative form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use present perfect to talk about actions that took place or began in the past and that are related to the present time. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You haven't understood what CRUD stands for. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When you use the <strong>negative</strong> form of the <strong>present</strong> <strong>perfect</strong>, you want to say that some action that is somehow expected to happen in the present or in the future did not start or did not take place in the past or before the moment of speaking.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In order to make a negative statement with present perfect, you use the following structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>subject + have/has + not + main verb (past participle) + complement</strong></p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Example:</p> <p><i>The IT engineer <b>hasn&rsquo;t finished</b> the database.</i></p> <p><i>I <b>haven&rsquo;t understood</b> what CRUD is.</i></p> <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Notice that it is more common to contract the auxiliary have/has with the negative particle NOT rather than with the subject.</p>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Contraction\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">I</span></br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">you</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">have not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">haven't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">he</span></br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">she</span></br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">it</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">has not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"</br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">hasn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">we</span></br><div class=\\\"center_text\\\">they</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">have not\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">haven't\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have not previously worked with databases."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Continuous Interrogative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">You can use the <strong>present continuous </strong>in its interrogative form to inquire about things that are happening at the moment of speaking.</p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Why are we using CRUD to create a database? "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">People also refer to the <strong>present continuous</strong> as the present progressive. You can use this tense to describe ongoing actions; that means, actions that are taking place at the moment of speaking or actions that are temporarily in progress in the present time.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In order to make an interrogative statement using the <strong>present continuous</strong>, use the following structure:</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>(wh- question word) + to be + subject + main verb + ing + complement + ?</strong></p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Examples:</p> <p><i>How <strong>are they programming</strong> the database?</i></p> <p><strong><i>Are you using</em></strong><i> CRUD functions to map the database?</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "How is CRUD improving storage?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "thus "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with this result; therefore"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Thus, throughout this section, we will briefly explain you what CRUD stands for. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mnemonic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a short word that summarizes several words  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can tell you it is a mnemonic for the four basic functions of persistent storage."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dispose of "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to delete or remove "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Update it or dispose of it."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "map "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to connect, match or link elements in a set"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: CRUD functions have improved storage by mapping SQL statements to make databases work. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "safe and sound"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "secure and without threats; unharmed  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Databases work safe and sound from possible threats."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hazard  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a threat or danger "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can automatically relate it to stored procedures, which prevents hazards such as, injection attacks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le01ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read about CRUD characteristics and functions "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a summary about CRUD, use your own words and paraphrase the information. Don't forget to use \u201cquotation marks\u201d to reference. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write five questions about CRUD and put them in a bag. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Interchange questions with your class mates about CRUD in a dynamic way. "}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read about CRUD characteristics and functions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a summary about CRUD."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I as about CRUD to my classmates."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I practice my pronunciation with my classmates in a dynamic way. "}]}]}